::U6PRE01::A risk factor {=can increase vulnerability without guaranteeing an outcome ~proves addiction ~always causes overdose ~cannot change}

::U6PRE02::Alcohol is {=a central-nervous-system depressant ~a vitamin ~an antibiotic ~only a stimulant}

::U6PRE03::Vaping devices produce {=aerosol that may contain nicotine and other substances ~only harmless water ~oxygen ~no particles}

::U6PRE04::THC may affect {=attention, reaction time, coordination, and judgment ~only product price ~only appetite ~no driving skill}

::U6PRE05::Taking another person's prescription is {=misuse ~appropriate use ~safe storage ~cessation}

::U6PRE06::An online pill's appearance {=cannot verify its contents ~proves its dose ~proves pharmacy origin ~guarantees safety}

::U6PRE07::The first action for an unresponsive person with abnormal breathing is {=call emergency services ~wait ~give food ~leave}

::U6PRE08::Naloxone {=can temporarily reverse opioid overdose but does not replace emergency care ~reverses every drug ~identifies fentanyl ~ends all monitoring}

::U6PRE09::An assertive refusal should be {=clear, direct, respectful, and supported by an exit plan ~vague and apologetic ~based on personal disclosure ~a long debate}

::U6PRE10::A credible health resource is {=qualified, current, and evidence-based ~the post with most likes ~an anonymous seller ~a rumor}
